WEBVTT

00:09.570 --> 00:12.360
It's starting to rain even harder now.

00:12.870 --> 00:15.360
I wonder if it will continue 
like this into the night.

00:15.930 --> 00:18.750
Abel hasn't returned yet, has he?

00:21.240 --> 00:23.040
Hey, I have something to tell you.

00:23.360 --> 00:24.600
I'm soaked!

00:24.600 --> 00:26.000
We can see that!

00:32.140 --> 00:33.630
Looks like I have a fever.

00:33.630 --> 00:35.960
Stop being so casual about it!

00:35.960 --> 00:38.430
This is because you do things 
like sleep by the fireplace.

00:38.430 --> 00:40.540
We have services now,

00:40.540 --> 00:43.110
but I'll be a little worried 
if no one is looking after you.

00:43.110 --> 00:46.470
No, no. I'll be just fine on my own.

00:46.470 --> 00:48.360
I'm not a child, after all.

00:48.360 --> 00:52.560
It isn't good to leave 
a sick person on their own!

00:52.560 --> 00:54.440
R-Right.

02:26.290 --> 02:30.000
Episode 3

02:26.290 --> 02:30.000
Lawrence's Concerns

02:40.630 --> 02:42.280
Pastor Lawrence?

02:42.280 --> 02:45.260
Where are the lady saint and Pastor Abel?

02:45.260 --> 02:46.420
Well, you see,

02:46.420 --> 02:51.200
Abel has caught a cold and
the lady saint is looking after him.

02:51.200 --> 02:52.190
What?

02:52.190 --> 02:53.640
Just the two of them?

02:53.640 --> 02:55.360
Won't that be a problem?

02:55.360 --> 03:00.350
I made their lunch before I came here, 
and I left them books to keep them quiet.

03:00.350 --> 03:03.360
<i>That's not what we're worried about.</i>

03:05.870 --> 03:08.810
<i>I wonder if the two of them 
are behaving themselves.</i>

03:08.810 --> 03:12.380
<i>Abel has to stay calm for
his own sake, but the lady saint...</i>

03:12.380 --> 03:15.120
I will tend to him!

03:16.130 --> 03:18.010
<b>Uneasy</b>

03:19.420 --> 03:20.650
Uneasy?

03:21.860 --> 03:24.760
Lady Saint, how is Abel feeling?

03:28.770 --> 03:31.900
Lady Saint, that isn't very dignified.

03:32.800 --> 03:34.680
Please, wake up.

03:35.920 --> 03:37.440
Scone...

03:38.520 --> 03:41.570
Now that you mention it, 
I haven't made them lately, have I?

03:42.200 --> 03:43.820
<i>Still...</i>

03:43.820 --> 03:47.320
<i>she seems entirely too 
defenseless in this situation.</i>

03:48.370 --> 03:49.830
<b>Uneasy</b>

03:55.060 --> 03:57.840
<i>It won't be good for her 
health to stay like this.</i>

03:57.840 --> 04:02.840
Lady Saint, there are members 
of the congregation nearby.

04:06.380 --> 04:07.840
Are they asking for me?

04:07.840 --> 04:09.000
I lied.

04:09.530 --> 04:11.980
It isn't good to lie!

04:11.980 --> 04:15.110
Under certain circumstances, 
sometimes it can't be helped.

04:15.110 --> 04:18.880
Then, am I allowed to lie 
when it can't be helped?

04:18.880 --> 04:20.110
I am, aren't I?

04:20.110 --> 04:23.690
Lady Saint, you aren't 
deft enough to lie, are you?

04:27.050 --> 04:28.760
Lawren, today you're...

04:29.860 --> 04:31.660
somehow...

04:34.480 --> 04:35.960
sterner than usual.

04:37.800 --> 04:40.550
I'm sorry! That wasn't my intention!

04:41.740 --> 04:44.470
There is something strange 
about me today, isn't there?

04:44.470 --> 04:46.790
Why would I take such 
an attitude toward the lady saint?

04:47.200 --> 04:49.400
Could it be that you have 
a cold, too, Lawren?

04:49.400 --> 04:52.080
There isn't anything wrong with my health.

04:52.080 --> 04:53.130
For now,

04:53.130 --> 04:56.760
I can promise that I won't do 
or say anything like that again.

04:56.760 --> 04:59.350
Are you really all right?

04:59.350 --> 05:00.280
Yes.

05:02.400 --> 05:05.620
Then, if the church has been closed up,

05:05.620 --> 05:07.820
it's all right for me to change clothes.

05:07.820 --> 05:09.650
I'll go back to my room for a moment.

05:15.640 --> 05:17.040
That was a mistake.

05:17.040 --> 05:18.920
You were awake this whole time?

05:19.360 --> 05:21.500
Why did I do that?

05:21.500 --> 05:25.750
<i>I think Lawrence understands 
far too little about himself,</i>

05:25.750 --> 05:27.980
<i>but this was my fault.</i>

05:28.380 --> 05:30.640
Yeah, what could've caused it?

05:30.640 --> 05:32.120
Do you think it's a cold?

05:32.120 --> 05:33.390
Probably not.

05:33.810 --> 05:35.810
The next day.

05:35.810 --> 05:37.680
I've baked scones!

05:37.680 --> 05:39.060
Scones!

05:39.060 --> 05:40.690
And I've made cookies, too.

05:40.690 --> 05:41.940
Cookies!

05:41.940 --> 05:43.610
There are madeleines, too!

05:43.610 --> 05:45.340
Madeleines!

05:45.340 --> 05:46.350
Wait.

05:46.350 --> 05:48.360
I made the lady saint cry.

05:48.360 --> 05:50.800
This is too much for me to eat.

05:49.600 --> 05:58.620
I made the lady saint cry.

05:50.800 --> 05:52.520
Please eat it.

05:52.520 --> 05:55.320
For him. Right now, he's
suffocating under all that guilt.

05:55.320 --> 05:56.920
Guilt?

05:56.920 --> 05:58.620
About what?

05:58.830 --> 06:01.640
<i>Both of them really are dense.</i>

06:03.490 --> 06:04.740
Lawrence.

06:05.390 --> 06:07.770
There's a letter from a classmate of ours.

06:08.170 --> 06:09.360
Thanks.

06:10.540 --> 06:12.900
Oh, that name brings back memories.

06:12.900 --> 06:16.100
Since you don't come to meetings, you're 
probably the only one who feels that way.

06:16.100 --> 06:18.520
What? You mean everyone else goes?

06:18.520 --> 06:21.170
We do, and we have normal 
conversations and everything.

06:21.020 --> 06:23.150
Jealous

06:21.170 --> 06:22.370
Jealous.

06:23.150 --> 06:25.170
I'd like to attend the meetings,

06:25.170 --> 06:27.650
but I can't leave 
the Lady Saint here on her own.

06:27.650 --> 06:29.820
Then why don't you bring 
Saint Cecilia along?

06:29.820 --> 06:32.280
You promised you wouldn't 
tell people about her.

06:32.280 --> 06:34.310
Just don't tell anyone she's a saint.

06:34.310 --> 06:36.870
Then how would I introduce her?

06:37.740 --> 06:38.570
Your little sister.

06:38.570 --> 06:40.530
Everyone knows I don't have one.

06:40.530 --> 06:41.960
A friend's daughter.

06:41.960 --> 06:43.210
That connection's too distant.

06:43.210 --> 06:45.400
A girl you picked up on the side 
of the road because she was lost.

06:45.400 --> 06:47.320
That invites too many 
misunderstandings, so no.

06:47.320 --> 06:50.550
Um, couldn't you just say 
I'm someone who's staying with you?

06:50.550 --> 06:54.250
Hmm, I feel like that would make 
them treat you too informally.

06:54.250 --> 06:58.690
I mean, to be honest, there's 
a really simple way to explain things.

06:59.520 --> 07:03.520
But if the two of you can't 
think of it yourselves...

07:03.520 --> 07:04.780
I'm not telling you!

07:04.780 --> 07:06.520
What does that mean?

07:07.220 --> 07:08.210
Huh?

07:08.210 --> 07:10.280
There's one here addressed 
to you, too, Abel.

07:10.280 --> 07:11.990
Oh, thank you.

07:11.990 --> 07:12.930
There.

07:12.930 --> 07:14.320
Hey!

07:14.320 --> 07:15.840
Why are you burning it?!

07:15.840 --> 07:17.310
Put that out right now!

07:17.310 --> 07:21.280
Abel, you have to treat 
collection letters with care,

07:21.280 --> 07:22.460
even if you can't pay them.

07:22.460 --> 07:24.330
You misunderstand me!

07:24.330 --> 07:26.880
This is just a letter from a friend.

07:26.880 --> 07:28.290
I'll go put it away.

07:28.510 --> 07:32.300
As usual, I have no idea what he's thinking.

07:33.220 --> 07:36.970
Lawren, you have 
a lot of friends, don't you?

07:38.360 --> 07:40.080
<i>Is it the letter?</i>

07:40.080 --> 07:42.770
<i>The lady saint must have a hometown,</i>

07:42.770 --> 07:44.850
<i>so it's possible that letters 
might arrive for her one day.</i>

07:45.350 --> 07:49.070
<i>If my blunder yesterday 
made her hate this place...</i>

07:49.070 --> 07:51.860
<i>and made her want to go back home, then...</i>

07:52.120 --> 07:53.000
<i>No.</i>

07:53.000 --> 07:55.200
<i>I won't do anything 
to trouble her ever again!</i>

07:55.200 --> 07:56.280
Lawren?

07:56.990 --> 08:00.950
What shall we do about 
this huge spread of sweets?

08:00.950 --> 08:02.920
<i>I've troubled her again today!</i>

08:04.120 --> 08:05.410
Lawren?

08:06.620 --> 08:08.100
I'm so sorry.

08:08.100 --> 08:11.430
Yesterday and today, all I've done is shown 
you the most unsightly sides of myself.

08:11.430 --> 08:15.010
When I thought that perhaps you 
had grown to hate living here,

08:15.010 --> 08:16.320
it made me too anxious to think straight.

08:16.320 --> 08:16.980
What?

08:16.980 --> 08:19.190
I would never grow to hate it here!

08:19.190 --> 08:20.140
But...

08:20.140 --> 08:23.820
Living here puts me more 
at ease than anywhere else.

08:24.600 --> 08:27.940
Every day, I'm so filled with happy 
thoughts about my life here...

08:27.940 --> 08:29.780
that I have no room to left to hate it.

08:29.780 --> 08:32.890
Have I made you feel 
that desperate in your everyday life?

08:32.890 --> 08:35.990
That's not what I mean!

08:36.290 --> 08:40.420
"I like living this way, 
with you looking after me,"

08:40.420 --> 08:42.700
"so please don't say such things."

08:42.700 --> 08:44.000
That's what I meant.

08:45.000 --> 08:46.580
I see.

08:46.900 --> 08:47.890
Huh?

08:47.890 --> 08:51.250
For some reason, that 
uneasy feeling I had is gone.

08:51.250 --> 08:53.830
Did you have heartburn?

08:53.830 --> 08:55.540
Perhaps I did.

08:57.010 --> 09:00.010
A string of heartburn.

09:00.270 --> 09:02.760
It sure is raining.

09:02.020 --> 09:04.020
The truth of that day.

09:04.630 --> 09:08.020
Oh, someone forgot this.

09:08.360 --> 09:11.510
It's already getting cold at night. 
Not having this will probably be problematic.

09:11.510 --> 09:13.900
Maybe I'll go and deliver it 
while I'm out shopping.

09:13.900 --> 09:15.790
You're going into the village? Alone?

09:15.790 --> 09:16.680
No,

09:16.680 --> 09:19.440
I think the lady saint will 
probably want to go along.

09:19.440 --> 09:21.520
So, I'll be here alone.

09:21.520 --> 09:24.620
Looking after things is boring. 
Maybe I'll go along, too.

09:24.620 --> 09:27.750
Now that I think about it, 
I haven't explored the village yet!

09:27.750 --> 09:30.840
When are you going back home?

09:30.840 --> 09:32.840
Are you going into the village?

09:33.710 --> 09:35.970
I would like to accompany you!

09:37.700 --> 09:40.000
Then, shall we leave right now?

09:40.000 --> 09:40.980
Yes!

09:41.870 --> 09:43.400
<i>Oh. This is...</i>

09:43.830 --> 09:45.640
<i>I'm gonna be in the way, right?</i>

09:46.040 --> 09:48.320
Lawrence, I think I'll stay here after all.

09:48.320 --> 09:49.680
What? You can't!

09:49.680 --> 09:52.280
I've already planned 
for you to carry everything for us!

09:52.280 --> 09:53.900
I can carry things, too!

09:53.900 --> 09:54.640
No, you can't.

09:54.640 --> 09:55.860
Apparently, I can't!

09:55.860 --> 09:58.580
Given the situation, Abel, 
you should come, too.

09:58.580 --> 10:01.710
You haven't looked around 
the village yet, have you?

10:03.890 --> 10:06.800
You won't think I'm in the way if I go?

10:06.800 --> 10:08.640
Why would I think that?

10:09.120 --> 10:11.800
You'll have less time with Lawrence.

10:11.800 --> 10:14.670
I'm always with Lawrence.

10:14.670 --> 10:17.560
Besides, lately, 
when Lawren is with you,

10:17.560 --> 10:19.830
I've been able to see 
a different side of him.

10:19.830 --> 10:21.810
It's quite a lot of fun!

10:21.810 --> 10:23.070
I see.

10:23.070 --> 10:25.800
So, that's the perspective of someone 
with a mania for Lawrence, huh?

10:26.390 --> 10:28.320
Are we going?

10:30.380 --> 10:32.400
Look, it's the lady saint.

10:32.400 --> 10:34.570
She's as beautiful as ever.

10:34.570 --> 10:37.210
She makes me feel like my own 
heart has been made clean.

10:37.560 --> 10:39.280
Scone...

10:37.570 --> 10:39.280
Droop

10:39.280 --> 10:41.120
And the pastor is with her.

10:41.120 --> 10:45.270
He's always so kind and he 
greets everyone with a smile.

10:45.270 --> 10:47.700
You skipped out on your 
work again, didn't you?

10:47.700 --> 10:51.720
Maybe it'd be better if you two 
just stayed here in the village.

10:51.720 --> 10:52.740
What?

10:53.860 --> 10:56.960
Where will you be delivering the lost item?

10:56.960 --> 10:59.380
I thought I would take it to their house.

10:59.380 --> 11:02.480
It's on the other side of the river, 
so we'll have to walk a good ways.

11:02.480 --> 11:07.220
Lawren, you've never taken me 
to the other side of the river, have you?

11:07.220 --> 11:10.480
Well, I don't want to 
make you walk too much.

11:10.480 --> 11:13.370
Saint Cecilia needs her 
exercise, too, you know?

11:13.370 --> 11:14.970
And you could just take a cart.

11:14.970 --> 11:16.160
Oh, that's true!

11:16.160 --> 11:18.120
Lady Saint!

11:18.730 --> 11:20.720
Would you like your fortune told?

11:20.720 --> 11:22.830
What? Um...

11:22.830 --> 11:26.200
I'm a fortune-teller who's barely 
making a living in this village.

11:26.200 --> 11:27.920
Are you interested in fortunes?

11:27.920 --> 11:30.200
Fortunes?

11:30.200 --> 11:32.660
I can do compatibility readings.

11:32.660 --> 11:34.360
I am a little curious.

11:34.360 --> 11:36.150
Now, Lady Saint.

11:36.150 --> 11:39.500
Don't solicit the lady 
saint of all people, please.

11:39.500 --> 11:41.370
Oh, but I'm in the service industry!

11:41.370 --> 11:43.470
I have to ask everyone, lady saint or not!

11:43.470 --> 11:46.270
You seem quite tenacious, 
but we'll be declining your offer.

11:46.270 --> 11:49.140
How unkind of you, pastor!

11:49.960 --> 11:55.450
I've made hardly any money 
again today! Oh, woe, woe, woe!

11:55.450 --> 11:56.950
L-Lawren...

11:57.420 --> 11:59.640
Now that we've heard that...

12:00.070 --> 12:02.280
<i>They sure are big softies.</i>

12:02.670 --> 12:04.590
Why me?

12:04.590 --> 12:07.200
I don't really like fortunes.

12:07.200 --> 12:08.640
Don't worry!

12:08.640 --> 12:10.650
Just think of it as something 
that could ease your mind.

12:11.560 --> 12:15.000
Has something happened lately 
that has improved your life overall?

12:15.920 --> 12:18.520
Protecting something so that 
it doesn't break is good,

12:18.520 --> 12:21.510
but you should probably take a look 
at your own footing, don't you think?

12:21.510 --> 12:24.520
Break? Are you making something?

12:24.520 --> 12:26.210
This looks like hard work.

12:26.210 --> 12:27.680
Doesn't it?

12:27.840 --> 12:29.610
Next, the lady saint.

12:29.610 --> 12:30.840
Yes?

12:31.360 --> 12:32.850
The one you await will not come.

12:32.980 --> 12:33.980
<b>The
one
you
await
will
not
come.</b>

12:33.970 --> 12:36.610
You must wait with dogged endurance.

12:36.770 --> 12:37.730
<b>Wait with
dogged endurance.</b>

12:37.720 --> 12:39.360
A new encounter will...

12:39.360 --> 12:41.530
Stop. Doctor's orders.

12:41.530 --> 12:44.150
Apparently, the one 
I'm waiting for won't come.

12:44.150 --> 12:45.620
W-Well...

12:45.620 --> 12:49.410
I'm sure that your current situation 
is already one of good fortune.

12:49.730 --> 12:53.420
And perhaps that's why no one 
else you're waiting for will come.

12:53.420 --> 12:55.040
I see.

12:55.040 --> 12:58.710
It's possible that the person I'm waiting 
for already arrived long ago.

13:00.700 --> 13:03.160
Last is the pastor, but...

13:03.800 --> 13:06.800
it seems your life will 
bring many ups and downs.

13:06.800 --> 13:08.920
I'm not sure I understand.

13:08.920 --> 13:11.050
Will something bad happen 
if things continue this way?

13:11.050 --> 13:12.470
Hmm.

13:12.470 --> 13:15.180
Well, you probably need to take a good look 
at those who are dear to you.

13:15.180 --> 13:17.020
Who could that be referring to?

13:17.810 --> 13:22.660
Maybe you should face the feelings 
of those around you and your own head-on.

13:22.660 --> 13:24.670
Am I not facing them already?

13:24.670 --> 13:25.800
Not at all.

13:26.570 --> 13:29.570
Thanks for the business! 
Come back again sometime!

13:29.810 --> 13:33.700
I request that next time the contents 
do not cause emotional distress.

13:33.700 --> 13:35.480
Oh, Lady Saint.

13:37.600 --> 13:40.120
Don't you want a compatibility reading?

13:43.270 --> 13:44.610
It's all right.

13:44.610 --> 13:50.120
I don't wish for such decisions to be
made by someone other than myself.

13:53.250 --> 13:55.350
What did you speak with her about?

13:57.870 --> 14:00.110
About my unwavering will.

14:00.110 --> 14:02.920
Oh, Lady Saint? We're going this way.

14:09.640 --> 14:11.870
Lady Saint, is something wrong?

14:11.870 --> 14:14.790
I tore my cape.

14:15.590 --> 14:17.660
Oh dear.

14:17.660 --> 14:18.720
If you'd like,

14:18.720 --> 14:21.630
you could come with me to a shop 
and choose something else to wear.

14:21.630 --> 14:24.680
Oh, but we have somewhere to be.

14:24.680 --> 14:26.260
We'd be very grateful!

14:26.260 --> 14:29.420
And while you're doing that, 
we'll go and deliver the lost item!

14:29.420 --> 14:30.430
What?

14:32.670 --> 14:37.050
<i>I never imagined that 
I'd be going off on my own.</i>

14:39.070 --> 14:40.960
Oh, if it isn't the lady saint!

14:40.960 --> 14:43.320
Hello! Can I help you with something?

14:43.320 --> 14:44.480
Hello.

14:44.480 --> 14:47.810
I'd like the lady saint 
to pick out something to wear.

14:47.810 --> 14:50.160
Her clothes got a little torn, you see.

14:50.160 --> 14:52.290
Oh, is that what's going on?

14:52.290 --> 14:55.530
Wait, the preach—the pastor isn't with you?

14:55.530 --> 14:58.320
I've been left behind.

14:58.320 --> 15:00.080
I see.

15:00.080 --> 15:01.340
"I see"?

15:01.340 --> 15:03.540
Now then, Lady Saint!

15:05.290 --> 15:07.100
What do you think of these clothes?

15:07.100 --> 15:08.390
Oh, instead of those...

15:10.130 --> 15:12.440
I think these clothes suit 
the lady saint better!

15:12.440 --> 15:14.390
Those are completely wrong!

15:16.150 --> 15:17.260
Now these are good.

15:17.260 --> 15:18.660
What are you talking about?

15:18.660 --> 15:21.060
I'm certain she prefers 
a cute style of clothing.

15:21.060 --> 15:23.270
Then these fit the bill exactly, don't they?

15:23.270 --> 15:27.070
The lady saint's clothing should give 
a tidy, clean impression!

15:27.070 --> 15:28.190
Wait right there!

15:28.190 --> 15:29.690
Clothes for the lady saint should be...

15:29.690 --> 15:33.690
Oh, honestly! No, the clothes 
I chose are better! Hold on!

15:30.400 --> 15:33.690
<i>I seem to have started a war.</i>

15:35.400 --> 15:39.450
Is this the correct way to wear this?

15:41.700 --> 15:43.420
Well done, everyone!

15:43.420 --> 15:44.890
This is a triumph of friendship!

15:44.890 --> 15:45.890
It really is...

15:45.890 --> 15:48.700
All my customers joined in.

15:48.700 --> 15:51.090
Women do like this kind of thing.

15:51.090 --> 15:52.700
Um...

15:53.130 --> 15:55.430
It doesn't look odd?

15:55.430 --> 15:58.180
Of course not! It looks really good on you.

15:59.400 --> 16:00.720
Now that I think about it...

16:00.720 --> 16:04.440
why were you unsurprised 
that Lawren didn't come?

16:04.440 --> 16:08.120
You see the phenomenon a lot 
at clothing stores.

16:08.120 --> 16:09.310
Phenomenon?!

16:09.310 --> 16:12.220
You should try asking him about it yourself, 
if you want to know more.

16:12.220 --> 16:14.320
Ask him for his opinion 
of those clothes, too.

16:14.540 --> 16:16.830
I-I will.

16:17.610 --> 16:21.820
Are you sure about leaving Saint 
Cecilia on her own like that?

16:23.680 --> 16:28.090
Have you ever been tossed into 
a situation like that on your own?

16:28.090 --> 16:29.340
No. Why?

16:30.930 --> 16:35.280
I experienced it once before 
when buying clothes for the lady saint.

16:35.280 --> 16:37.230
I didn't belong there.

16:38.350 --> 16:42.300
Still, that's no reason to force her 
to stay behind like that.

16:42.300 --> 16:43.500
What're you gonna do?

16:43.500 --> 16:45.930
What if she walks around 
the village alone and

16:45.930 --> 16:48.360
comes back saying, "I found a handsome man!"

16:48.870 --> 16:50.360
If that happens...

16:51.770 --> 16:54.760
I will have to determine 
whether the man is worthy of her.

16:54.760 --> 16:56.400
What are you, her father?

16:56.720 --> 16:58.020
Oh!

16:58.020 --> 17:00.920
This is the wedding dress 
from before, isn't it?

17:00.920 --> 17:02.200
Yes, it is.

17:02.200 --> 17:04.810
Now, I wonder when I'll be 
able to make yours, Lady Saint.

17:04.810 --> 17:06.790
N-Not yet!

17:06.790 --> 17:08.170
"Not yet," is it?

17:08.170 --> 17:10.050
Oh, no, I mean...

17:10.050 --> 17:13.140
You teased me last time, too.

17:13.960 --> 17:15.280
I'm sorry.

17:15.280 --> 17:17.920
You two just seem so happy, 
I can't help myself.

17:19.240 --> 17:20.300
"Two"?

17:20.300 --> 17:23.800
That boy, the pastor. 
I mean he seems happy, too.

17:24.340 --> 17:28.070
Before you came here, 
he always seemed lonely somehow.

17:28.070 --> 17:30.710
He put up a front 
of being mature and content,

17:30.850 --> 17:33.400
but maybe he longed for a normal family.

17:33.730 --> 17:38.160
But he isn't like that anymore, 
so I worry a little less for him.

17:38.160 --> 17:40.240
A normal family?

17:40.240 --> 17:44.270
He didn't have parents. 
He was raised by his grandfather.

17:44.270 --> 17:47.550
So, ever since his grandfather 
died, he's been alone.

17:47.930 --> 17:49.290
Alone.

17:50.450 --> 17:53.290
I was alone, too.

17:55.470 --> 17:56.900
I see.

17:56.900 --> 17:58.800
Then you both must be very happy.

17:59.800 --> 18:00.960
Yes.

18:00.960 --> 18:02.180
Mom.

18:02.680 --> 18:04.180
I finished the deliveries.

18:04.440 --> 18:06.480
Why are there so many people here?

18:06.480 --> 18:07.930
Thanks for doing that!

18:08.200 --> 18:11.440
Lady Saint, this is 
the son I mentioned before.

18:11.970 --> 18:13.600
Pleased to meet you!

18:14.420 --> 18:15.360
Hi.

18:16.360 --> 18:19.370
Hey! Introduce yourself properly!

18:19.370 --> 18:21.580
<i>Is this a normal family?</i>

18:25.280 --> 18:27.240
Well, the lady saint has left.

18:27.240 --> 18:29.180
We should leave, too.

18:29.180 --> 18:31.830
You could buy something first.

18:39.850 --> 18:41.240
Now that I think about it,

18:41.240 --> 18:44.840
I don't know where the house 
that Lawren and Able went to is.

18:44.840 --> 18:46.840
I remember that he said 
it's across the river...

18:50.110 --> 18:53.360
Could that be the river he meant?

18:53.360 --> 18:56.610
If I get closer, then Lawren will...

18:59.360 --> 19:01.860
Oh! Are you all right?

19:02.100 --> 19:04.660
I feel like my leg might cramp.

19:07.380 --> 19:09.280
Thank you.

19:09.280 --> 19:11.420
You aren't hurt anywhere, are you?

19:11.420 --> 19:13.660
No, I'm all right!

19:14.750 --> 19:17.430
Have you come from another village?

19:17.430 --> 19:20.430
Yes, I came here looking for someone.

19:20.430 --> 19:23.810
Then, if there's anything 
I can do to help...

19:23.810 --> 19:26.240
I have a good idea of where to look.

19:26.240 --> 19:28.640
I think my search will be over quickly.

19:28.640 --> 19:30.490
I see.

19:30.490 --> 19:32.840
I'm sorry I couldn't be of any help.

19:32.840 --> 19:36.900
If you're from this village, 
then maybe we'll meet again.

19:36.900 --> 19:38.040
Bye, then.

19:39.060 --> 19:41.280
Watch your footing, all right?

19:41.910 --> 19:43.380
I will.

19:45.200 --> 19:47.990
<i>So she's on a journey.</i>

19:48.350 --> 19:51.180
<i>She seemed very elegant somehow.</i>

19:51.180 --> 19:53.950
<i>I wonder what the person 
she's looking for is like.</i>

19:53.950 --> 19:55.200
Lady Saint?

19:55.760 --> 19:56.960
Lawren!

19:57.380 --> 19:59.910
Did you deliver the lost item?

19:59.910 --> 20:00.790
Yes.

20:00.790 --> 20:02.970
You could have waited at the store.

20:02.970 --> 20:06.200
Everyone chose these clothes for me!

20:06.200 --> 20:07.280
What do you think?

20:07.280 --> 20:09.230
Let's see...

20:09.230 --> 20:10.610
You seem cold.

20:11.220 --> 20:14.290
<i>Why? Why oh why?</i>

20:15.230 --> 20:18.040
Wow, Saint Cecilia, that looks great on you!

20:18.040 --> 20:19.250
Right, Lawrence?

20:19.250 --> 20:20.240
Abel!

20:20.240 --> 20:22.380
The people who picked them 
out have great fashion sense!

20:22.380 --> 20:24.240
Abel!

20:25.160 --> 20:26.650
Yes, of course!

20:26.650 --> 20:28.550
They look very nice on you, Lady Saint.

20:28.990 --> 20:33.250
But they don't seem very warm, 
so let's finish our shopping quickly.

20:37.160 --> 20:41.170
<i>Lawren is always distant 
at times like these.</i>

20:41.170 --> 20:43.600
<i>I... want more!</i>

20:46.650 --> 20:48.050
Lady Saint?

20:49.230 --> 20:53.560
Th-They look nice... and that's all?

20:58.070 --> 21:01.160
I-I think you look lovely.

21:02.010 --> 21:03.380
Really?

21:03.380 --> 21:04.780
Really.

21:04.780 --> 21:07.160
May I ask you to let go of me now?

21:07.560 --> 21:09.120
Yes!

21:12.530 --> 21:17.500
<i>For the lady saint to pursue 
an opinion regarding herself this ardently...</i>

21:17.500 --> 21:19.790
<i>I don't think she's done that very often.</i>

21:19.790 --> 21:23.550
<i>Saying things like this aloud is difficult.</i>

21:23.550 --> 21:25.390
<i>He seems the straight-forward type,</i>

21:25.390 --> 21:28.800
<i>but he actually can't 
say what he really thinks.</i>

21:29.640 --> 21:32.520
If you mean the church, 
it's up on that hill.

21:33.050 --> 21:35.320
There. You can just see it 
in the distance, right?

21:35.320 --> 21:39.230
Is it true that there is a lady saint there?

21:39.230 --> 21:40.430
It is.

21:40.430 --> 21:42.360
She lives with the pastor.

21:42.360 --> 21:43.450
I see.

21:43.450 --> 21:45.380
Thank you for your kindness.

21:45.920 --> 21:48.220
I'm thinking of going to see her.

21:48.880 --> 21:51.790
I want to see what kind of person 
this village's lady saint is.

23:23.280 --> 23:25.300
A lost item in the church.

23:25.300 --> 23:27.620
This is the fifth time 
it's happened since I came.

23:27.620 --> 23:31.100
This scarf belongs to the lady 
who lives across the river!

23:31.100 --> 23:34.020
And it's the fifth time you've 
known who the item belongs to.

23:34.020 --> 23:37.830
Why don't you ever turn those powers 
of observation toward Saint Cecilia?!

23:37.830 --> 23:39.490
Did you say something?
